module dropletDepositionDetection
module nimsImagingDetection

manifest CelE_CBM3a_Enzyme
manifest G4_Substrate_Probe
manifest PhosphateBuffer_pH6
manifest AcetateBuffer_pH5
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant
manifest DextromethorphanStandard
manifest UniversalMALDI_Matrix

// ============================================================
// On-chip Integration of Droplet Microfluidics and
// Nanostructure-Initiator Mass Spectrometry for Enzyme
// Screening. Heinemann et al., Lab on a Chip, 2016.
// DOI: 10.1039/c6lc01182a
//
// Platform: uNIMS -- integrates a digital microfluidics (DMF)
// chip (electrowetting-on-dielectric, EWOD) with a patterned
// NIMS array (640 pads, 5x5 cm silicon wafer) for time-resolved
// enzyme kinetics via mass spectrometry imaging.
//
// PROTOCOL OVERVIEW:
//   PART 1: Dextromethorphan (DXM) standard deposition to
//           validate microfluidic droplet actuation onto NIMS
//           pads. 150 nL droplets actuated over NIMS pads;
//           MS imaging confirms analyte sorption at m/z 272.
//
//   PART 2A: CelE kinetics at pH 6 (phosphate buffer, 50 mM).
//            G4 substrate-probe reacted with CelE-CBM3a.
//            Droplets incubated at 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 min
//            (parallel loading, 6 pads per time point).
//            Degradation products G3, G2, G1 monitored by
//            MS imaging. Fractional conversion readout.
//
//   PART 2B: CelE kinetics at pH 5 (acetate buffer, 100 mM).
//            Same enzyme/substrate; continuous series loading.
//            Time points: 10, 20, 40 min.
//            Result: similar product distribution to pH 6;
//            CelE is robust across both pH conditions.
//
// DEVICE DETAILS:
//   - Microfluidics chip: glass substrate, 128 chrome electrodes
//     (5 cm L x 500 um W x 375 um H), 5 um SU-8-5 dielectric,
//     PDMS fluidics channel (500 um W x 225 um H), 31 digital
//     arrayers aligned to NIMS pads.
//   - T-junction for droplet generation: pressure-driven flow,
//     ~150 nL droplets in HFE-7500 immiscible oil phase.
//   - Dropbot control: 20 V hold, 90 V / 10 kHz fast actuation
//     (250 ms bursts) for droplet movement in/out of pockets.
//   - NIMS array: ICP-RIE etched silicon nanostructures
//     (DRIE, SF6/O2 30/20 ratio, -80 C, 6 mTorr), patterned
//     with photopatternable PDMS (3% benzophenone, 10:1 ratio).
//   - Reversible PDMS seal between DMF chip and NIMS array
//     allows removal for MS imaging on ABSciex 5800 MALDI-TOF
//     (positive mode, laser intensity 4150, focus m/z 1200,
//     50 um laser step, universal MALDI matrix 20 mg/mL MeOH).
//   - Analysis: OpenMSI spot set analysis.
//
// DROPLET VOLUMES:
//   All droplets ~150 nL (unit). 6 uL plugs broken into
//   droplets at t-junction (0.05 uL/s reaction cocktail,
//   0.2 uL/s HFE-7500 oil phase). BioScript `dispense 1 units`
//   abstracts the 150 nL droplet throughout.
//
// TEMPERATURE: All reactions at room temperature (25 C).
//   `heat` statements model incubation timing on NIMS pads.
//
// FRACTIONAL CONVERSION QUANTIFICATION:
//   Signal normalised as [G1]/([G4]+[G3]+[G2]+[G1]) etc.
//   This internal normalisation eliminates sensitivity to
//   droplet volume variation (device maintains +/-10% SD in
//   droplet size; turbulent mixing at t-junction causes
//   initial larger droplets).
//
// NOTE ON SURFACTANT INTERFERENCE:
//   HFE-7500 + surfactant stabilises droplets but suppresses
//   NIMS ionisation; MS imaging (not spot analysis) was used
//   to detect all degradation products. NIMS surface acts as
//   capture substrate; probe (fluorous-tagged) and products
//   remain adsorbed after droplet removal. Surfactant
//   adherence to NIMS surface negatively impacts sensitivity.
//   Future directions: NIMS-compatible surfactants.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- DXM validation + pH6 kinetics +
//                             pH5 kinetics (all dispense/mix/heat)
//   BB2  validationPass    -- depositionSignal > 0: DXM confirmed
//                             on NIMS pads; dispose and continue
//   BB3  validationFail    -- depositionSignal <= 0: no analyte
//                             sorption; drain DXM droplets
//   BB4  validationJoin    -- join: pH6 kinetics branch begins
//   BB5  pH6Pass           -- pH6Signal > 0: valid kinetics
//                             detected; dispose all pH6 droplets
//   BB6  pH6Fail           -- pH6Signal <= 0: no product signal;
//                             drain all pH6 droplets
//   BB7  pH6Join           -- join: pH5 kinetics branch begins
//   BB8  pH5Pass           -- pH5Signal > 0: valid kinetics;
//                             dispose all pH5 droplets
//   BB9  pH5Fail           -- pH5Signal <= 0: no product signal;
//                             drain all pH5 droplets
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals;
//                             NIMS array removed for MS imaging
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 - STEP 1: Prepare HFE-7500 oil phase.
//   Novec HFE-7500 (3M, US) with 100 uL Picoglide surfactant
//   pumped through channel for 30 min to coat PDMS surface.
//   Oil phase separates aqueous droplets at t-junction and
//   maintains droplet integrity during EWOD actuation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 - STEP 2: Dispense dextromethorphan standard.
//   1 mg/mL DXM in H2O. Used for rudimentary testing of
//   microfluidic functions and NIMS array evaluation.
//   150 nL droplet dispensed from syringe (prefilled 5 uL plug).
//   DXM detects at m/z 272 (H+) -- matrix-free ionisation
//   confirmed; no ionisation on surrounding structures.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dxmDroplet = dispense 1 units of DextromethorphanStandard

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 - STEP 3: Generate DXM droplets at t-junction.
//   Aqueous DXM plug broken into ~150 nL droplets by
//   immiscible HFE-7500 oil phase at t-junction.
//   Droplet synchronisation matches droplet formation with
//   electrode actuation for uniform spacing.
//   `mix` abstracts the t-junction droplet generation event.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

dxmDropletInOil = mix dxmDroplet with oilPhase for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 - STEP 4: Load DXM droplets onto NIMS pads.
//   Flow stopped; 20 V hold on electrodes. Droplets actuated
//   onto uNIMS pads (90 V, 10 kHz, 250 ms bursts) and
//   incubated to allow DXM to sorb onto NIMS surface.
//   `heat` at 25 C models room-temperature sorption contact.
//   After sorption, droplets ejected from pocket.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat dxmDropletInOil at 25c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 - STEP 5: Coat NIMS array with universal MALDI matrix.
//   20 mg/mL MeOH universal MALDI matrix applied to NIMS
//   array after removal from uNIMS system. Required for
//   ABSciex 5800 MALDI-TOF MS imaging.
//   `mix` abstracts matrix co-crystallisation step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

maldiMatrix = dispense 1 units of UniversalMALDI_Matrix
dxmNimsArray = mix dxmDropletInOil with maldiMatrix for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 1 - STEP 6: MS imaging QC -- DXM deposition detection.
//   nimsImagingDetection module abstracts ABSciex 5800
//   MALDI-TOF MS imaging (50 um laser step, m/z 272 ion map).
//   OpenMSI spot set analysis confirms DXM deposition pattern.
//   QC gate: signal > 0 confirms successful analyte sorption
//   onto uNIMS pads (not surrounding structures).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

depositionSignal = detect nimsImagingDetection on dxmNimsArray for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: DXM validation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): depositionSignal > 0 -> DXM detected on NIMS
//             pads; dispose and proceed to kinetics branch.
// Fail (BB3): depositionSignal <= 0 -> no sorption (surfactant
//             suppression or actuation failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (validationJoin).
// ============================================================

if (depositionSignal > 0) {
    dispose dxmNimsArray
} else {
    drain dxmNimsArray
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: validationJoin
// Dispose DXM deposition QC signal. Control falls into
// pH 6 kinetics branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose depositionSignal

// ============================================================
// PART 2A: CelE Kinetics at pH 6 (phosphate buffer, 50 mM)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2A - STEP 1: Prepare enzyme/substrate reaction mix.
//   Reaction premixed off-chip in 0.5 mL eppendorf tube:
//     4 uL phosphate buffer (50 mM, pH 6) +
//     1 uL G4 substrate-probe (1,4-beta-D-cellotetraose-probe,
//       MW 1515.48, formula C55H78F17N5O24, detected at m/z
//       1516.43 H+) +
//     1 uL CelE-CBM3a (240 ug/mL endoglucanase, GH5 domain
//       from C. thermocellum Cthe_0797 fused to CBM3a).
//   Final volume: 6 uL plug drawn into syringe tubing.
//   BioScript: each component dispensed as 1 unit; merged to
//   form reaction cocktail. Buffer is the major volume component.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Three buffer units to approximate 4:1:1 volume ratio
// (4 uL buffer : 1 uL substrate : 1 uL enzyme).
// Compiler requires explicit sequential merging of multi-unit
// buffer volumes; chained mix accumulates 3+1=4 buffer units.

ph6_buf1 = dispense 1 units of PhosphateBuffer_pH6
ph6_buf2 = dispense 1 units of PhosphateBuffer_pH6
ph6_buf3 = dispense 1 units of PhosphateBuffer_pH6
ph6_buf4 = dispense 1 units of PhosphateBuffer_pH6

ph6_buf_12   = mix ph6_buf1 with ph6_buf2 for 5s
ph6_buf_34   = mix ph6_buf3 with ph6_buf4 for 5s
ph6_bufBulk  = mix ph6_buf_12 with ph6_buf_34 for 5s

ph6_substrate = dispense 1 units of G4_Substrate_Probe
ph6_enzyme    = dispense 1 units of CelE_CBM3a_Enzyme

ph6_subBuf   = mix ph6_substrate with ph6_bufBulk for 10s
ph6_reactionCocktail = mix ph6_subBuf with ph6_enzyme for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2A - STEP 2: Generate reaction droplets at t-junction.
//   6 uL plug injected at 0.05 uL/s reaction cocktail,
//   0.2 uL/s HFE-7500 oil to generate ~150 nL droplets.
//   Central fluidics chamber filled with droplet train.
//   Flow stopped (syringe pump halted); 20 V electrode hold.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase_pH6 = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
ph6_dropletsInOil = mix ph6_reactionCocktail with oilPhase_pH6 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2A - STEP 3: Parallel loading onto uNIMS pads.
//   All 31 arrayer electrodes actuated simultaneously.
//   Droplets loaded in parallel onto NIMS pads (Fig. 4A).
//   Incubation times: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 min over six
//   successive pad positions (6 pads per time point).
//   At each interval, 6 droplets synchronously ejected from
//   pocket into central chamber and evacuated.
//   G4 substrate (m/z 1516) degraded to:
//     G3 cellotriose-probe   (m/z 1354, C49H68F17N5O19)
//     G2 cellobiose-probe    (m/z 1192, C43H58F17N5O14)
//     G1 glucose-probe       (m/z 1030, C37H48F17N5O9)
//   `heat` blocks model the sequential incubation time points.
//   Room temperature (25 C) throughout.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Time point 1: 10 min incubation
heat ph6_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// Time point 2: 20 min incubation (cumulative)
heat ph6_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// Time point 3: 30 min incubation (cumulative)
heat ph6_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// Time point 4: 40 min incubation (cumulative)
heat ph6_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// Time point 5: 50 min incubation (cumulative; final time point)
heat ph6_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2A - STEP 4: Coat NIMS array with MALDI matrix.
//   After all time points completed, uNIMS chip removed from
//   system. NIMS array coated with universal MALDI matrix
//   (20 mg/mL MeOH). Mounted in ABSciex 5800 MALDI-TOF.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

maldiMatrix_pH6  = dispense 1 units of UniversalMALDI_Matrix
ph6_nimsArray    = mix ph6_dropletsInOil with maldiMatrix_pH6 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2A - STEP 5: MS imaging and kinetics detection.
//   ABSciex 5800 MALDI-TOF; positive ionisation; 50 um step.
//   OpenMSI spot set analysis; fractional conversion:
//   [G1]/([G4]+[G3]+[G2]+[G1]) for each time point pad.
//   nimsImagingDetection abstracts the full MS imaging scan
//   and OpenMSI analysis of G4, G3, G2, G1 product map.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ph6Signal = detect nimsImagingDetection on ph6_nimsArray for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: pH 6 kinetics QC gate
// Pass (BB5): ph6Signal > 0 -> G3/G2/G1 hydrolysis products
//             detected by MS imaging; dispose all pH6 droplets.
// Fail (BB6): ph6Signal <= 0 -> no product signal (surfactant
//             suppression or enzyme inactivity); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (pH6Join).
// ============================================================

if (ph6Signal > 0) {
    dispose ph6_nimsArray
} else {
    drain ph6_nimsArray
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: pH6Join
// Dispose pH 6 kinetics QC signal. Control falls into
// pH 5 kinetics branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose ph6Signal

// ============================================================
// PART 2B: CelE Kinetics at pH 5 (acetate buffer, 100 mM)
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2B - STEP 1: Prepare enzyme/substrate reaction mix.
//   Same as PART 2A but with 100 mM acetate buffer (pH 5).
//   Reaction premixed off-chip: 4 uL acetate buffer +
//   1 uL G4 substrate-probe + 1 uL CelE-CBM3a (240 ug/mL).
//   Result: CelE produces similar product distributions at
//   pH 5 and pH 6, demonstrating robustness to process
//   conditions (reaction profile consistent with Deng, 2015).
//   pH 5 run loaded continuously in series (Fig. 4B).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ph5_buf1 = dispense 1 units of AcetateBuffer_pH5
ph5_buf2 = dispense 1 units of AcetateBuffer_pH5
ph5_buf3 = dispense 1 units of AcetateBuffer_pH5
ph5_buf4 = dispense 1 units of AcetateBuffer_pH5

ph5_buf_12  = mix ph5_buf1 with ph5_buf2 for 5s
ph5_buf_34  = mix ph5_buf3 with ph5_buf4 for 5s
ph5_bufBulk = mix ph5_buf_12 with ph5_buf_34 for 5s

ph5_substrate = dispense 1 units of G4_Substrate_Probe
ph5_enzyme    = dispense 1 units of CelE_CBM3a_Enzyme

ph5_subBuf          = mix ph5_substrate with ph5_bufBulk for 10s
ph5_reactionCocktail = mix ph5_subBuf with ph5_enzyme for 10s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2B - STEP 2: Generate reaction droplets at t-junction.
//   Continuous series loading used for pH 5 run (Fig. 4B).
//   6 uL plug injected; droplets removed from pad directly
//   from flow (Supplementary Video). HFE-7500 oil phase
//   separates droplets during continuous series actuation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPhase_pH5      = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
ph5_dropletsInOil = mix ph5_reactionCocktail with oilPhase_pH5 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2B - STEP 3: Series loading; incubation time points.
//   Droplets loaded continuously in series onto NIMS pads.
//   Time points: 10, 20, 40 min (three time points for pH 5).
//   At each time point, droplets ejected and fresh droplets
//   actuated into pocket for next incubation interval.
//   G4 degradation to G3, G2, G1 monitored as for pH 6.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Time point 1: 10 min incubation
heat ph5_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// Time point 2: 20 min incubation (cumulative)
heat ph5_dropletsInOil at 25c for 10m

// Time point 3: 40 min incubation (cumulative)
heat ph5_dropletsInOil at 25c for 20m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2B - STEP 4: Coat NIMS array with MALDI matrix.
//   uNIMS chip removed; NIMS array coated with universal
//   MALDI matrix. Re-mounted in ABSciex 5800 MALDI-TOF.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

maldiMatrix_pH5 = dispense 1 units of UniversalMALDI_Matrix
ph5_nimsArray   = mix ph5_dropletsInOil with maldiMatrix_pH5 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PART 2B - STEP 5: MS imaging and kinetics detection.
//   Same MS imaging and OpenMSI analysis as PART 2A.
//   Fractional conversion at each time point compared to pH 6.
//   nimsImagingDetection abstracts full MALDI-TOF scan.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ph5Signal = detect nimsImagingDetection on ph5_nimsArray for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: pH 5 kinetics QC gate
// Pass (BB8): ph5Signal > 0 -> G3/G2/G1 hydrolysis products
//             detected by MS imaging; dispose all pH5 droplets.
// Fail (BB9): ph5Signal <= 0 -> no product signal; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ph5Signal > 0) {
    dispose ph5_nimsArray
} else {
    drain ph5_nimsArray
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose pH 5 kinetics QC signal. Experiment complete.
// NIMS array removed from uNIMS system and placed in
// ABSciex 5800 MALDI-TOF for final MS imaging.
// Each NIMS array supports up to 20 enzyme/condition assays
// (31 pads per run; 640 pads total; scalable to 620 assays
// at 1 pad/enzyme with modified protocol).
// ============================================================

dispose ph5Signal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
